N5008 [class.mi]/4-5: D : B, C with B and C both derived non-virtually from
A has two A subobjects; `B::i' / `C::i' ([class.mi]/5) and the conversions
to B& and C& ([conv.ptr]/3) each designate one of them.  The front end
rejected the class ("non-virtual base class tag-A inherited multiple
times").  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its
WRONG assertion.
